+## Pitfalls
+
+- **Plan too abstract** — if the implementer has to guess file paths or code structure, the plan fails. Every task needs exact paths and complete code.
+- **Tasks too large** — anything over 5 minutes of work should be split. Large tasks hide failures and make TDD impossible.
+- **Missing test commands** — every task that produces code needs exact test commands with expected output, not just "test it works".
+- **Forgetting the baseline** — if the plan modifies existing code, include a step to run existing tests FIRST to establish the baseline.
+- **No commit step** — every task should end with a commit. Plans without commits produce monolithic changes that are hard to review.
+- **YAGNI violations in plans** — don't add "flexible" abstractions for hypothetical future needs. Plan only what's needed now.
+- **Wrong sibling skill** — if the user wants a quick throwaway experiment, use `spike`. If they want a formal plan saved to `.hermes/plans/`, use `plan`. This skill is for implementation plans that will be executed.
+
